{#
  CalendarView macro — a calendar: a week, a rolling four weeks, or a
  padded month, with previous/next/today navigation, a view switcher,
  APG grid keyboard navigation, a picked day, disabled days and
  consumer-rendered events per day.

  HTML tag: <div> (root) wrapping a toolbar, a <table role="grid"> built
            from @lilydesignsystem/nunjucks-headless's calendar-table
            macro family, and one aria-live status region.
  CSS class: calendar-view
  Companion runtime: calendar-view.client.js

  The macro renders the SSR skeleton only: the toolbar, an empty grid and
  the status region. Which days appear depends on civil-date arithmetic
  that lives in the client (the same arithmetic date-time-picker's client
  exports), so calendar-view.client.js builds the weekday header and the
  day cells, exactly as gantt-chart.client.js builds the gantt grid body.
  Call `initCalendarView(root, opts)` (or `autoInit(opts)`) once.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  NUNJUCKS DEVIATIONS from the canonical Svelte props
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  A macro cannot evaluate a callback, so every function-valued prop is a
  calendar-view.client.js init option rather than a macro param:
    events, isDisabled, onNavigate, onDayClick, onEventClick, renderDay,
    labels.previous(view), labels.next(view), labels.periodAnnouncement,
    labels.weekday, labels.weekdayAbbr, labels.day.
  Plain strings stay macro params: labels.weekView / fourWeekView /
  monthView / today / weekNumberHeader.
  Range options are client init options too: ranges (marked ranges, each day
  inside gets data-range="{kind}"), selectedRange, onRangeSelect, and
  labels.weekNumber(week) / labels.rangeAnnouncement(start, end). `labels.previousLabel` / `labels.nextLabel` are
  fixed strings naming the two arrows before hydration; once the client
  runs, `labels.previous(view)` / `labels.next(view)` replace them.

  Typed event fields, inline editing and export (0.5.0) are client options and plain-string labels:
    Client init options: eventFields (array of {id, header, type?, options?, parse?, exportValue?, exportable?, editable?,
      editLabel?, numberFormat?, dateFormat?} — functions are allowed here, it is client code), read from each event's `values`;
      onFieldEdit({eventId, fieldId, value, previous}) (an agenda field is editable only when it is set: the client can see its
      own option), exportFilename ("calendar"), exportScope ("period" or "all"), onExport(file) (return false to take over the
      download); labels.editAnnouncement(eventTitle, fieldHeader, text), labels.editInvalid(eventTitle, fieldHeader),
      labels.exportAnnouncement(format, eventCount, filename). `renderDay` / `renderAgendaDay` get `fieldText(event, fieldId)`.
      The client fires `fieldedit` and `exportfile` on the root too.
    Macro params: labels.export, labels.exportCsv / exportTsv / exportExcel (plain strings; each gates its button) and
      labels.exportHeaders (an object of plain strings, {title, start, end}); none of the buttons renders without it. The
      client reads the headers from the root's `data-lily-calendar-view-export-headers`.

  Params (single `opts` object):
    label       — string, required. aria-label for the grid.
    view        — "day" | "week" | "four-week" | "month" | "agenda", default "month".
                  "agenda" lists the month's days that have events as a plain list.
    agendaEmptyDays — boolean. Agenda view: also list days with no events.
    anchorDate  — ISO date the period is computed around. Default: `today`.
    selectedDate— ISO date already picked.
    today       — ISO date; never computed here (SSR-safe).
    minDate, maxDate — ISO dates bounding what can be picked.
    locale      — BCP 47, picks the first day of the week.
    labels.search — plain string: renders a search field; the client shows only the events whose title and field text
                  contain every typed word (case, diacritics, word order ignored), marks the match in the title and
                  announces the count (client labels.searchAnnouncement(matched, total)). `search` is its start value.
                  Escape clears it. Client options: eventCompare(a, b) orders a day's events; onCopy({ text, rowCount });
                  labels.copy (a plain string) adds a button that puts the export on the clipboard.
    showPeriodTitle — boolean. Renders the period-title placeholder between the
                  arrows; the client fills it from `labels.periodTitle(view, start, end, anchorDate)`.
    hideOutsideDays — boolean. Month view: days outside the month stay empty.
    weekendDays — array of weekday numbers (0 = Sunday); those cells get data-weekend.
    selectionMode — "single" (default) or "multiple" (a click or Enter toggles a day;
                  the client keeps the days: getSelectedDates / setSelectedDates).
    maxEvents   — number. Cap per day; the client shows "+N more" (labels.moreEvents).
    moveEvents  — boolean. Event drag-and-drop and Alt+arrow keys (client option
                  onEventMove, or the `eventmove` event); also on when onEventMove is set.
    dayView     — via labels.dayView: a switcher button for the one-day view.
    showWeekNumbers — boolean. Add an ISO week-number column (a row header per
                  week); `labels.weekNumberHeader` is its header text.
    labels      — object, see above. Every field optional; each gates
                  the control it names.
    name        — string, default "calendar". Discriminator for ids.
    id          — string, default "calendar-view-{name}".
    classes     — string. Extra CSS classes on the root <div>.
    attributes  — object. Extra HTML attributes spread onto the root.

  Usage:
    {% from "./calendar-view.njk" import calendarView %}
    {{ calendarView({
      label: "Appointments", view: "month", anchorDate: "2026-01-15",
      today: "2026-01-08",
      labels: { monthView: "Month", weekView: "Week", today: "Today" }
    }) }}

  Spec: spec/index.md.
#}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/calendar-table/macro.njk" import calendarTable %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/calendar-table-head/macro.njk" import calendarTableHead %}
{% from "lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless/components/calendar-table-body/macro.njk" import calendarTableBody %}

{%- macro calendarView(opts) -%}
{%- set labels = opts.labels | default({}) -%}
{%- set name = opts.name | default("calendar") -%}
{%- set id = opts.id | default("calendar-view-" + name) -%}
{%- set view = opts.view | default("month") -%}
{%- set anchorDate = opts.anchorDate | default(opts.today) | default("1970-01-01") -%}
{%- set tableHtml = calendarTable({ label: opts.label, classes: "calendar-view-table", attributes: {"role": "grid"}, html: (calendarTableHead({ html: "" }) ~ calendarTableBody({ html: "" })) | safe }) -%}
<div
  class="calendar-view{% if opts.classes %} {{ opts.classes }}{% endif %}"
  id="{{ id }}"
  data-lily-calendar-view-root
  data-lily-calendar-view-name="{{ name }}"
  data-lily-calendar-view-view="{{ view }}"
  data-lily-calendar-view-anchor-date="{{ anchorDate }}"
  {%- if opts.selectedDate %} data-lily-calendar-view-selected-date="{{ opts.selectedDate }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.today %} data-lily-calendar-view-today="{{ opts.today }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.minDate %} data-lily-calendar-view-min-date="{{ opts.minDate }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.maxDate %} data-lily-calendar-view-max-date="{{ opts.maxDate }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.locale %} data-lily-calendar-view-locale="{{ opts.locale }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.hideOutsideDays %} data-lily-calendar-view-hide-outside-days{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.weekendDays %} data-lily-calendar-view-weekend-days="{{ opts.weekendDays | join(',') }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.selectionMode %} data-lily-calendar-view-selection-mode="{{ opts.selectionMode }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.maxEvents is defined and opts.maxEvents is not none %} data-lily-calendar-view-max-events="{{ opts.maxEvents }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.agendaEmptyDays %} data-lily-calendar-view-agenda-empty-days{% endif %}
  data-lily-calendar-view-label="{{ opts.label }}"
  {%- if labels.exportHeaders %} data-lily-calendar-view-export-headers="{{ labels.exportHeaders | dump }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.moveEvents %} data-lily-calendar-view-move-events{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.showWeekNumbers %} data-lily-calendar-view-show-week-numbers{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.showWeekNumbers and labels.weekNumberHeader %} data-lily-calendar-view-week-number-header="{{ labels.weekNumberHeader }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if opts.attributes %}{% for k, v in opts.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
{%- if opts.showPeriodTitle or labels.dayView or labels.weekView or labels.fourWeekView or labels.monthView or labels.agendaView %}
<div class="calendar-view-toolbar">
<div class="calendar-view-switcher" role="group">
{%- if labels.dayView %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-switcher-button calendar-view-switcher-button-day" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if view == 'day' else 'false' }}" data-lily-calendar-view-switch="day">{{ labels.dayView }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.weekView %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-switcher-button calendar-view-switcher-button-week" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if view == 'week' else 'false' }}" data-lily-calendar-view-switch="week">{{ labels.weekView }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.fourWeekView %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-switcher-button calendar-view-switcher-button-four-week" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if view == 'four-week' else 'false' }}" data-lily-calendar-view-switch="four-week">{{ labels.fourWeekView }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.monthView %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-switcher-button calendar-view-switcher-button-month" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if view == 'month' else 'false' }}" data-lily-calendar-view-switch="month">{{ labels.monthView }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.agendaView %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-switcher-button calendar-view-switcher-button-agenda" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if view == 'agenda' else 'false' }}" data-lily-calendar-view-switch="agenda">{{ labels.agendaView }}</button>{% endif %}
</div>
<div class="calendar-view-nav">
<button type="button" class="calendar-view-previous-button"{% if labels.previousLabel %} aria-label="{{ labels.previousLabel }}"{% endif %} data-lily-calendar-view-previous>&#8249;</button>
{%- if opts.showPeriodTitle %}<span class="calendar-view-title" data-lily-calendar-view-title></span>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.today %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-today-button"{% if not opts.today %} disabled{% endif %} data-lily-calendar-view-today-button>{{ labels.today }}</button>{% endif %}
<button type="button" class="calendar-view-next-button"{% if labels.nextLabel %} aria-label="{{ labels.nextLabel }}"{% endif %} data-lily-calendar-view-next>&#8250;</button>
</div>
</div>
{%- endif %}
{%- if labels.search %}
<input type="search" class="calendar-view-search" aria-label="{{ labels.search }}" value="{{ opts.search | default('') }}" data-lily-calendar-view-search>
{%- endif %}
{%- if labels.exportHeaders and (labels.copy or labels.exportCsv or labels.exportTsv or labels.exportExcel) %}
<div class="calendar-view-export" role="group"{% if labels.export %} aria-label="{{ labels.export }}"{% endif %} data-lily-calendar-view-export-group>
{%- if labels.copy %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-export-button" data-calendar-export-format="copy" disabled>{{ labels.copy }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.exportCsv %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-export-button" data-calendar-export-format="csv" disabled>{{ labels.exportCsv }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.exportTsv %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-export-button" data-calendar-export-format="tsv" disabled>{{ labels.exportTsv }}</button>{% endif %}
{%- if labels.exportExcel %}<button type="button" class="calendar-view-export-button" data-calendar-export-format="xlsx" disabled>{{ labels.exportExcel }}</button>{% endif %}
</div>
{%- endif %}
{{ tableHtml | safe }}
<div class="calendar-view-status" id="{{ id }}-status" aria-live="polite" data-lily-calendar-view-status></div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
